WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.209
For about seventy days, embalmers worked in sheltered workshops.

00:00:05.209 --> 00:00:15.220
They cleansed the body, dried it with natron salts, anointed it with precious oils, and wrapped it layer by layer in linen.

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:28.000
Between the folds they placed amulets of protection, and over it all, priests recited spells — so the body would endure and the person would be recognized.

